1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:01,300
The rice is cut.

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,667
The clock starts.

3
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,100
In north India,

4
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,933
farmers have only a few

5
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:07,667
weeks between the paddy

6
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:09,900
harvest and sowing wheat.

7
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:12,833
The field has to be cleared.

8
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:14,100
And the straw

9
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,000
left behind is bulky,

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,600
loose,

11
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,567
and slow to move.

12
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,967
Without a baler,

13
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:20,667
a buyer,

14
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:21,600
or a truck,

15
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,600
the fastest option is a matchstick.

16
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,567
That is why the smoke

17
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:28,200
comes back every autumn.

18
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:29,867
Now,

19
00:00:29,867 --> 00:00:31,233
the same straw,

20
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:32,700
with a plan.

21
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:34,967
The harvest ends.

22
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:36,300
A baler arrives

23
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,067
and packs the straw.

24
00:00:38,067 --> 00:00:39,133
Within days,

25
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:41,400
an aggregator picks it up.

26
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,033
The field is clear

27
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:45,000
in time for wheat.

28
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:47,033
The straw becomes pellets.

29
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:48,100
The pellets go

30
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,400
to a plant that needs them.

31
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:51,600
Same field.

32
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,633
Same few weeks.

33
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,267
A different ending.

34
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:56,300
What decides it is whether

35
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,167
the farmer can find a baler

36
00:00:58,167 --> 00:00:59,933
and a buyer in time.

37
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:02,733
IndiaBiomass is building that connection.
